<Shell>
 <section><h2>A network economy, explored from the inside.</h2><p>The vision is a coordinated network of autonomous people and firms. Participants can bring customer trust, commercial work, specialist capability, reusable assets or operating responsibility. Different projects can assemble different combinations of those contributions.</p><p>Intent’s proposed operating layer connects qualification, agreements, architecture, shared tooling and delivery accountability. Each engagement still needs an identifiable customer, payer, responsible lead and affordable budget. Membership alone creates no ownership, voting or earnings entitlement.</p><Figure svg={networkEconomy({id:'financial-atlas-entry'})} caption="Possible paths into work. A relationship, repository, class or provider introduction must still become an authorized opportunity with a real payer. This is a design to test, not evidence of a contracted pipeline." /></section>
 <section><h2>Start with the question your group is asking.</h2><p>Read the chapters in order for a full workshop. For a focused call, open a chapter, choose an example and expand its diagram. Presentation view reduces the site navigation; left and right arrow keys move between chapters when focus is outside a control.</p><ol class="econ-journey">{chapters.map((c,i)=><li><span class="chapter-count">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h2><a href={chapterPath(c.id)}>{c.title}</a></h2><p>{c.summary}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
 <section class="econ-split econ-rule-block"><div><h2>What is real here?</h2><p>The <a href="/estate/">operating atlas</a> links the company’s practice, public artifacts, learning, tools and products. These financial pages explore ways that connected work could support paid contributions and sustainable delivery.</p></div><div><h2>What is still a design?</h2><p>The network economics, role schedules, example prices and participation structures. A real agreement requires actual scope, rights, capacity, authority and terms. A good model makes those choices visible rather than implying they have already been made.</p></div></section>
</Shell>
